{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_244","type":"agent_message","text":"The holiday diagnosis found a strong effect: during scheduled NYSE closures, equity perpetuals still trade, but their cash-session volatility is about one quarter of a normal weekday’s. That estimate is stable when individual closure dates are left out. Separately, the simple volatility mixture improved every asset/configuration cell in the July and November confirmation windows; the more complex quantile model has not clearly beaten it."}}
