{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_350","type":"agent_message","text":"The gold regression has an explanation: the robust seasonal profile makes the quiet-weekend variance estimate too small for the squared-return estimator. A few real Sunday moves then inflate Monday’s entire forecast. I’m testing a general fix that keeps the original volatility estimate and uses the robust profile only to distribute uncertainty over future times."}}
