{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_439","type":"agent_message","text":"The shock-cap idea fails its first check: similar states in earlier data were already broadly calibrated, and the two largest HYPE errors account for only about 0.007% of the broad one-hour score. I’m dropping that rule. The next test changes the training target so high-volatility session minutes carry more weight, matching their larger contribution to CRPS."}}
