{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_450","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat >> agent/journal.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Iteration 29 — calibrate a stale volatility state, not just its interface\n\n**Hypothesis.** The missing-data-safe EWMA renormalizes its surviving weights. When all recent observations are absent, this freezes the last short-term volatility estimate rather than aging it. A volatile state observed hours ago may be less informative than the slower daily forecast.\n\n**Change.** Stress the current candidate with trailing three-hour and twelve-hour NaN gaps, leaving the real scoring paths intact. Never fill the gap or invent a return across it. For crypto1, compare the unchanged stale forecast against log-scale interpolation toward the same model's daily latent scale, with predeclared decay half-lives of one and six hours. Calendar allocation and the innovation law stay fixed; no price-center correction is introduced. This branch is exactly inactive with a complete context.\n\n**Result.** Pending official CRPS over all four general windows.\n\n**Verdict.** Retain a gap-only correction only if it improves both development and confirmation by at least 0.5% under both gap durations, with most asset-window cells improving. Otherwise report the stress loss and keep the original estimator. The serving contract remains mandatory regardless of scoring gains.\n\n**Lesson.** Pending.\nEOF\nuv run agent/run_variants.py gap_reference3h gap_decay1h_3h gap_decay6h_3h gap_reference12h gap_decay1h_12h gap_decay6h_12h --model gap_models --suffix general --workers 2 --configs crypto1 --ends 2026-07-20 2026-08-24 2026-10-12 2026-11-08 --details > agent/results/gap_general.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_484","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat agent/empirical_models.py && uv run python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\nfor p in Path('agent/results').glob('empirical*/suite.json'):\n rows=json.loads(p.read_text());v={}\n for h in [3600,86400]:\n  r=[x for x in rows if x.get('time_length')==h]\n  if r:v[h]=sum(x['mean_crps']*x['num_prompts'] for x in r)/sum(x['num_prompts'] for x in r)\n print(p.parent.name, v)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_484","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat agent/empirical_models.py && uv run python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\nfor p in Path('agent/results').glob('empirical*/suite.json'):\n rows=json.loads(p.read_text());v={}\n for h in [3600,86400]:\n  r=[x for x in rows if x.get('time_length')==h]\n  if r:v[h]=sum(x['mean_crps']*x['num_prompts'] for x in r)/sum(x['num_prompts'] for x in r)\n print(p.parent.name, v)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"\"\"\"Symmetric, context-derived innovation laws with a learned forecast scale.\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport os\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nfrom scipy.special import ndtr\n\nfrom ml_features import finite_ewm\nfrom ml_models import scale_adjustment\nfrom seasonal_models import forecast_variance, get_profile, seasonal_values\n\nCONTEXT_DAYS = 7\nVARIANT = os.environ.get('SYNTH_RESEARCH_VARIANT', 'empirical_standard')\n\n\ndef empirical_quantiles(asset, start, step, context, uniforms, standardize=True):\n    # A regular index makes absent rows explicit NaNs. No prices are filled.\n    index = pd.date_range(context.index[0], context.index[-1], freq='1min')\n    frame = context.reindex(index)\n    p = np.asarray(frame.close, dtype=float)\n    good = np.isfinite(p) & (p > 0)\n    logp = np.full(len(p), np.nan)\n    np.log(p, out=logp, where=good)\n    k = step//60\n    r = np.r_[np.full(k, np.nan), logp[k:]-logp[:-k]]\n    complete = pd.Series(good.astype(float)).rolling(k+1, min_periods=k+1).sum().to_numpy() == k+1\n    r[~complete] = np.nan\n    table = get_profile(asset, str(context.index[-1].date()), 'America/New_York')\n    season = seasonal_values(index, table, 'America/New_York')\n    r /= np.sqrt(pd.Series(season).rolling(k, min_periods=k).sum().to_numpy())\n    phase = pd.Timestamp(start).minute % k\n    select = np.flatnonzero(np.asarray(index.minute) % k == phase)\n    values = r[select]\n    if standardize:\n        prior = np.sqrt(finite_ewm(values*values, 720/k, len(values)))\n        prior = np.r_[np.nan, prior[:-1]]\n        values = values/np.maximum(prior, 1e-7)\n        values = np.clip(values, -15., 15.)\n    ages = np.asarray((index[-1]-index[select]).total_seconds())/60\n    use = np.isfinite(values)\n    values, ages = values[use], ages[use]\n    if len(values) < 60:\n        return None\n    weights = np.exp2(-ages/4320)\n    # Symmetry keeps the conditional center at zero and preserves the atom\n    # from real flat candles. This is a distribution, not a price-gap repair.\n    values = np.r_[values, -values]\n    weights = np.tile(weights, 2)\n    mean_abs = np.sum(weights*np.abs(values))/weights.sum()\n    if mean_abs < 1e-12:\n        return None\n    values *= np.sqrt(2/np.pi)/mean_abs\n    order = np.argsort(values)\n    values, weights = values[order], weights[order]\n    coordinates = (np.cumsum(weights)-.5*weights)/weights.sum()\n    return np.interp(uniforms, coordinates, values)\n\n\ndef simulate(asset, start_time, time_increment=300, time_length=86400,\n             num_simulations=1000, context_prices=None):\n    seed = int(os.environ.get('SYNTH_BENCHMARK_SEED', '20261108'))\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    last, stepvar = forecast_variance(asset, start_time, time_increment, time_length, context_prices)\n    adjustment = scale_adjustment(asset, start_time, time_length, context_prices, 'vol', 1.)\n    normal = rng.normal(size=(num_simulations, len(stepvar)+1))\n    z = empirical_quantiles(asset, start_time, time_increment, context_prices,\n                            ndtr(normal), standardize=VARIANT != 'empirical_raw')\n    if z is None:\n        z = normal\n    if VARIANT == 'empirical_mix':\n        eta = .4\n        z *= np.exp(eta*rng.normal(size=num_simulations)-.5*eta*eta)[:, None]\n    z[:, 0] = 0.\n    z[:, 1:] *= np.sqrt(stepvar)*adjustment\n    paths = last*np.exp(np.cumsum(z, axis=1))\n    return (start_time, time_increment, *paths.tolist())\nempirical_mix_dev {3600: 982.4127534961942, 86400: 2893.6940313160385}\nempirical_standard_dev {3600: 982.6825469228365, 86400: 2892.5573737719455}\nempirical_raw_dev {3600: 987.6491798595962, 86400: 2896.0116632029144}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
