{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_537","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat .gitignore agent/suggestions.md'","aggregated_output":"# The agent is told to commit often, so anything huge and regenerable must be excluded here:\n# a `git add -A` would otherwise commit a multi-GB .venv (torch + CUDA on GPU campaigns) and\n# 1000-path prediction files at ~5.5MB each. Committed weights are the exception — the champion\n# must stay runnable offline, so DO NOT add model artifacts to this list.\n.venv/\n__pycache__/\n*.pyc\nminer_outputs/\nmarket_data/\nagent/cache/\nagent/BUDGET.md\n# Suggestions outside this model's scope\n\n- Expose interval-level CRPS details in the official backtest result. The validator already computes them; retaining them avoids instrumentation and makes price-versus-volatility diagnosis easier.\n- Preserve the calendar's distinction between precise release timestamps and coarse earnings session anchors in the production interface. A date can be known while its exact release minute remains uncertain.\n- Report valid realized-price coverage and missed-prompt counts alongside mean CRPS. Sparse references and unanswered prompts must remain visible when comparing models.\n- Document the issuance lead and candle close convention next to the serving interface. Here the context ends three minutes before a 24h prompt and two minutes before a 1h prompt.\n\nNo operator miner models were encountered or used. All implementation ideas and fitted artifacts in this campaign use the allowed public scoring code, supplied snapshot/calendar, and this campaign's own research.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_538","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"uv run python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport pandas as pd\nfor tag in ['candidate_calendar_wide_field','candidate_shape_wide_field','linear_raw_dev','linear_blend_dev','deep_raw_dev','deep_blend_dev','candidate_calendar_events','event_slow_events','event_halfslow_events']:\n    d=pd.DataFrame(json.loads((Path('agent/results')/tag/'suite.json').read_text()))\n    d['config']=['crypto1' if h==3600 else 'crypto24' if a in ['BTC','ETH','SOL','XRP','HYPE'] else 'other24' for a,h in zip(d.asset,d.time_length)]\n    print(tag, d.groupby('config').apply(lambda x: (x.mean_crps*x.num_prompts).sum()/x.num_prompts.sum(),include_groups=False).round(6).to_dict())\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
